 # Conditional Slicing Mechanism
-Also called: Conditional 3D Gaussian Slicing, 7DGS Conditioning
 
 ## Overview
-The Conditional Slicing Mechanism conditions a 7-dimensional Gaussian (defined over spatial, temporal, and angular dimensions) on observed time $t$ and view direction $d$ to yield a conditional 3D Gaussian governing the spatial component [S1]. This operation "slices" the full 7D distribution to integrate temporal dynamics and view-dependent effects into the traditional 3D rendering pipeline without introducing additional temporal dependencies in the spherical harmonics [S1]. It sets itself apart from static Gaussian Splatting variants by explicitly modeling the joint distribution of space, time, and view, allowing the spatial mean and covariance to shift based on the current rendering context [S1].
