 ## How it works
 **Inputs:**
-*   Base Gaussian parameters: spatial mean $\mu_p$, temporal mean $\mu_t$, directional mean $\mu_d$, base opacity $\alpha$, scaling factors $\lambda_t, \lambda_d$.
-*   Covariance structure: Lower-triangular matrix $L$ such that $\Sigma = LL^\top$, or the partitioned blocks $\Sigma_{(t,d)}$, $\Sigma_{p,(t,d)}$, $\Sigma_p$.
-*   Context variables: Observed time $t$, view direction $d$.
-*   Optional refinement features: Feature vector $f$ (if adaptive refinement is applied).
